      "rationale": "L1 and L2 both explicitly state that HiBiT was inserted into the 'first extracellular loop' of endogenous GLUT4 via CRISPR/Cas9 knock-in. The topology landmarks place ECL1 at residues 46\u201381 (36 aa), flanked by TM1 (24\u201345) and TM2 (82\u2013103). No specific junction residue is named in either clip, so the site is region-level. The endogenous knock-in context and successful insulin-stimulated surface translocation assay establish surface_and_function validation. L3\u2013L5 (same PMC12309902 group) independently confirm surface-accessible HiBiT-GLUT4 with ~120-fold insulin response, corroborating ECL1 as the tag location. CRISPR/Cas9 knock-in of the HiBiT coding sequence into the endogenous GLUT4 locus in mice, placing HiBiT within the first extracellular loop (ECL1, residues 46\u201381). Primary brown adipocytes from these mice were used to study GLUT4 surface translocation by luminescence complementation.",
