  "literature_notes": "All seven ledger lines converge on ECL1 (residues 46\u201381) as the sole validated extracellular insertion site for GLUT4. The other five extracellular spans are too short or lack any ledger support: ECL2 (133\u2013135, 3 aa), ECL3 (193\u2013201, 9 aa), ECL4 (309\u2013322, 14 aa), ECL5 (375\u2013379, 5 aa), and ECL6 (443\u2013446, 4 aa) are all unsupported by any ledger line. The N-terminus (1\u201323) and C-terminus (467\u2013509) are both intracellular, ruling out terminal extracellular tags. L3/L4/L5 (PMC12309902) describe HiBiT-GLUT4 constructs with confirmed surface luminescence (~1000-fold over control, ~120-fold insulin response) but do not independently name ECL1; they are treated as corroborating evidence for the L1-grounded ECL1 site rather than a separate site. The two sites reported differ in tag type (HiBiT vs. Myc) and primary publication, justifying separate entries per the instructions.",
